  "answer": "1 known distant body recovered blind(s); the strongest has S/N 14.8 with a distance of about 111 AU (epoch bootstrap 68% range 100.0 to 142.9 AU; at 95% the far side is unbounded). A candidate at most, not a discovery. Detects movers from 50 AU outward. A distance needs S/N x (1/d) large enough: in a 15-day visit within about 120 AU at the S/N 8 threshold and about 200 AU for an Eris-bright body; within about half that in a 10-day visit (scaled from the measured Eris profile). Farther bodies are detected but not ranged. One visit reaches only about 0.6 magnitudes fainter than Eris: about V 19.3 for an Eris-coloured body, about V 20.7 for a Sedna-coloured one (scaled from Eris at S/N 14.3 and Sedna at forced S/N 7.5). That is about 2 magnitudes shallower than Pan-STARRS (V 21.5) and than Planet Nine's predicted brightness, so this search cannot test Planet Nine or Planet X.",
